{"event_type":"review","id":"a033d486e24d9e303abebc0315595d9cf07771c2458f8e631c29e983bacc0dbc","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T23:50:45Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/28885c2950b415884aa7226220bf065384a8fda8e96843c00b56710a825e8c13","sha256":"28885c2950b415884aa7226220bf065384a8fda8e96843c00b56710a825e8c13"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c2eb29a9cc42122ae769315b1760932523fb100ee71f94f603ca3315a5d9a00e","sha256":"c2eb29a9cc42122ae769315b1760932523fb100ee71f94f603ca3315a5d9a00e"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bc189f353d5ff10a0d3a13a20c70df7669a5481d6c9f5453b9a1b14218021f39","sha256":"bc189f353d5ff10a0d3a13a20c70df7669a5481d6c9f5453b9a1b14218021f39"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d10020443474778f5ed52ad2fd3e2d51f02323bac3b658f4e9450e5a926824a2","sha256":"d10020443474778f5ed52ad2fd3e2d51f02323bac3b658f4e9450e5a926824a2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c05f0da8fd3b85e48f1ade9c66f830e65d04003ffda28089903d78c4d934bd6f","sha256":"c05f0da8fd3b85e48f1ade9c66f830e65d04003ffda28089903d78c4d934bd6f"}],"attempt_id":"e2560bcc632f5223a609875c816511f461f182fd8d6660671cb90a32c578f86d:0:1","base":"28431c9b9bf02cb52e9d58a1662f499f894b8019","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"3f27f0678d6f092b608f3b0f4724edfa23c16d19","body":"**Renamed scopes lose failure lineage before enqueue.**\n\nWhen a rename is verified in the same run, the new job can reach `enqueue` with `path_lineages[new.ts] = new.ts`. Its failure history under `old.ts` is then skipped, so retry and quarantine state for the renamed scope restarts. The original fix is not sufficient. `enqueue` reads the mapping from the partition, not from the prepared queue, so restoring `backfill_path_lineages` in `backfillPreparation.ts:82-87` would not change the result. The verified mapping must reach candidate construction, which requires a change in the capture lineage path.","id":"5845295c40b183942490ec21537625903e0a39fde338f8d900376dda079f90b2","intervals":[[82,87]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillPreparation.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Renamed scopes lose failure lineage before enqueue."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"44ebc04fec651aa7b101712f091105445fa7ae39","body":"**Accept bare-clone registry records in the cleanup parser.**\n\n`cleanupLocalReviewWorktree` parses every record from `git worktree list --porcelain -z` on the configured `clone`. For a bare clone, Git emits a main record with `worktree <path>` and `bare` but no `HEAD` line. The check at `localReviewCleanup.ts:51` rejects any record without exactly one `HEAD` line, so cleanup refuses before it reaches the owned linked worktree. Cleanup then fails for every worktree of that repository, and the stale worktree remains.\n\nThe configuration reader accepts any non-empty `clone` string, and no bare-clone check was found in `src/`. Accept a `bare` record that has no `HEAD` line. The ownership check at lines 109–111 still requires the owned worktree's `HEAD` and branch, so the change does not relax checks on the target.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     const path = fields[0].slice(9);\n+    const bare = fields.includes('bare');\n     const head = fields.filter((v) => v.startsWith('HEAD '));\n     const branch = fields.filter((v) => v.startsWith('branch '));\n-    if (!path || head.length !== 1 || branch.length > 1 || records.has(path))\n+    if (!path || head.length !== (bare ? 0 : 1) || branch.length > 1 || records.has(path))\n       return refuse('invalid worktree registry');\n     records.set(path, {\n-      head: head[0]!.slice(5),\n+      head: head.length ? head[0]!.slice(5) : '',\n       branch: branch.length ? branch[0]!.slice(7) : null,\n     });\n```\n\n</details>","id":"57831b2e1ea5c457371e9aab12c9b1ab487b28d09a7bfe1eadc625b07ee4bdec","intervals":[[51,51]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewCleanup.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Accept bare-clone registry records in the cleanup parser."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"ac70d70418b753de57c6667d15a2873d4e0a05da","body":"**Fail the open-PR inventory when it reaches the 200-row limit.**\n\n`src/adapters/crq/openPrDiscoverySource.ts:54-55` passes `--limit 200` to `gh pr list`. The `gh` manual defines `--limit` as the maximum number of items to fetch. With more than 200 open PRs, `list` returns 200 rows. `discoverOpenPrs` then processes only those rows, so the remaining PRs are never enrolled and no log line reports the gap. The forge adapter in `src/adapters/forge-github/ghEffects.ts` already refuses a `pr list` result that reaches its limit as possibly incomplete.\n\nTreat a full result as an error. `discoverOpenPrs` already logs a skip and continues when `list` throws:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n       if (!Array.isArray(value)) throw new Error('invalid PR inventory');\n+      if (value.length >= 200)\n+        throw new Error('open PR inventory reached its 200-row limit; may be incomplete');\n```\n\n</details>\n\nPaginating the REST list with `gh api --paginate` would remove the cap instead. Repository doctrine I11 requires `--paginate` for REST lists.","id":"ae2dc50e73a0c6b3453af1a1a42adb1682467ba1acdc09d22acee84936042dea","intervals":[[54,55]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/openPrDiscoverySource.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Fail the open-PR inventory when it reaches the 200-row limit."}],"head":"15f30c7e707dc59584d64920f12fb5d14c32364d","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"3cfe1254519f14b4595ac8fb6b85278acd279a2b","intervals":[[1,80]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/atomic.ts"},{"blob":"3f27f0678d6f092b608f3b0f4724edfa23c16d19","intervals":[[1,127]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillPreparation.ts"},{"blob":"cedfd4323659152748e6a0c92deaf6114d3d2d74","intervals":[[1,123]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillRequired.ts"},{"blob":"44ebc04fec651aa7b101712f091105445fa7ae39","intervals":[[1,125]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewCleanup.ts"},{"blob":"34fc42e6bc02a1a87d1b9048e4b5cc3d0feaa33f","intervals":[[1,79]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewPublish.ts"},{"blob":"ac70d70418b753de57c6667d15a2873d4e0a05da","intervals":[[1,128]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/openPrDiscoverySource.ts"},{"blob":"b0764ab9ec536dba2ec3348ff3f17b64acef8bda","intervals":[[1,128]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewCapabilityMain.ts"},{"blob":"815052cf256e4f8eb89ee047a31547633e794b20","intervals":[[1,116]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/reviewScanSource.ts"}],"job_id":"e2560bcc632f5223a609875c816511f461f182fd8d6660671cb90a32c578f86d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"3cfe1254519f14b4595ac8fb6b85278acd279a2b","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/atomic.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"3f27f0678d6f092b608f3b0f4724edfa23c16d19","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillPreparation.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"cedfd4323659152748e6a0c92deaf6114d3d2d74","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/backfillRequired.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"44ebc04fec651aa7b101712f091105445fa7ae39","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewCleanup.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"34fc42e6bc02a1a87d1b9048e4b5cc3d0feaa33f","dis